id: pm-rlm-bx9v
title: Reuse explicitly selected verified subanswers across runs
description: "Opt-in cross-run reuse built on existing digests and core ledger records. Acceptance: matching source scope, snapshot, question, tool/model policy and consent identities reuse with zero new model calls; changing one source revision invalidates only dependent results; retain original provenance without double-counting usage. Provide typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals and remedies, README/example, non-git public-tracker validation, seeded model-based state tests and concurrency interleavings."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T00:07:55.801Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T01:17:30.054Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Matching explicitly selected source scope, snapshot, question, tool/model policy and consent identities reuse a prior subanswer with zero new model calls.; Changing one source revision invalidates only dependent selected results. Independent subanswers remain reusable.; Reuse reports original run/call provenance and original usage separately, with no double-counted new charges."
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T00:09:03.255Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: core CLI supplies certified full reads, native item/history transactions and locks, not verified model subanswer reuse. pm-rlm prompt digests reuse within a run; replay verifies recorded work. pm-memory embedding caches and purpose consent are distinct; pm-context freshness manifests invalidate packet sections but do not authenticate RLM answers; pm-swarm coordinates native resources. Implement an explicit selected-call reuse command atop existing checkpoint records, immutable snapshots, replay verification and SDK CAS. Identity is opt-in at original execution, freezes history access, and binds tool/model policy plus consent revision. No cache discovery or implicit reuse."
  "2026-10-26T00:22:09.768Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit selected original-call reuse, opt-in immutable policy/consent identities, native checkpoint provenance, zero new usage and bounded CLI previews. Native resume/replay reverify provenance. Root dependencies cover scope membership; child dependencies cover supplied source rows. Foreign rows skip with a remedy. Public-tracker copy measurement: 23 public items, 2 scoped, 3 original logical calls / 5 scripted protocol requests, 2 reused subanswers / 0 new requests, one changed revision caused one dependent refusal while one independent child reused, new counters all zero, compact JSON 944 bytes; source archive unchanged. Fixture validates protocol and provenance, not model quality. First publication interleavings passed 10 before/after boundaries; native custom-status and peer-completion tests added."
  "2026-10-26T00:35:23.852Z",codex-agent,"Validation progress: 500 seeded checkpoint operation sequences passed against exact SDK-read state, preserving CRLF/whitespace inputs and native relationships while replaying older snapshots. The final sequence generator also exercises legacy-v1 input to v2 publication; full CI will rerun all 500. One non-git tracker passed peer transitions at all 82 dynamically traced source/target/storage lease, load, save, materialization, completion and unlock boundaries (83 tests including the parent). Custom randomized status registries, peer success/started targets and pending-intent recovery are covered. Linked pm test run: node --test test/reuse.test.ts passed 7/7. Targeted reuse source coverage measured 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; full npm and Bun release gates remain CI work. Native test-result tracking was disabled, so results are recorded here without changing its policy."
  "2026-10-26T00:42:06.857Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changed only the snapshot branch in the equality guard so snapshot changes were accepted; node --test --test-name-pattern='one source revision invalidates' test/reuse.test.ts failed with Missing expected rejection for dimension snapshot. Restored the exact source bytes afterward. Added a deterministic real-filesystem stale-release interleaving (SDK operations remain real): pause after old ownership is read, race a second release and a new peer lease; serialized cleanup passed 1/1. Full boundary interleavings passed 83/83 (82 injected boundaries plus parent), and CLI/SDK linked tests passed 7/7."
  "2026-10-26T00:44:48.583Z",codex-agent,"Lease-cleanup revert proof passed: restored only the former unlocked release callback, retaining the rest of the feature. The deterministic real-I/O regression failed because the stale callback deleted the newer peer lease (ENOENT). Restored the exact source and retained the positive 1/1 proof. The property model now interchanges native v1 and v2 checkpoint inputs, alternates parent/dependency relationships through SDK updates, samples unchanged native ledger fields against an SDK-read reference, and replays older snapshots against current target revisions. No new importer, sync format or content-only idempotency key was introduced. CI must certify the final full source scope at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T00:48:45.451Z",codex-agent,"Ready for CI release-gate validation. Final local typecheck, lint, duplication (0 percent), docstring gate (32 files, 140 declarations), generated changelog and changelog check passed. Added strict output usage validation: all accounting coordinates are finite bounded integers; reused roots require one logical call and exactly zero new charges, independently of original informational provenance. Both request and output extremes are exercised. Recovery/peer/duplicate-release targeted checks passed 3/3 after restoring source; model-independent state and concurrency fixtures use real SDK trackers. Publishing the feature branch and a ready PR; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-26T00:53:01.789Z",codex-agent,"PR 28 is ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/28 . Feature commit b9456f4. PR CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40251216452 and explicit full npm/Bun release-gate dispatch https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40251216664 are running. Health, identity, typecheck, lint, duplication, build and docstrings passed in both Node 22 and 26 jobs; full coverage is in progress. Automated review is not approval evidence: CodeRabbit skipped automatic review and Sourcery reported quota exhaustion; no review was requested through a mention."
  "2026-10-26T00:53:40.834Z",codex-agent,"Local operational note: pinned pm health reports the installed pm-github extension was built for host 2026.10.25 while this repository pins SDK 2026.10.20. Clean CI health passed on Node 22 and 26, and all history/integrity checks passed locally. The dependency pin and local extension configuration were retained per scope. This version-skew diagnostic is separate from feature acceptance and clean-install CI evidence."
  "2026-10-26T01:00:23.275Z",codex-agent,"Initial CI full coverage passed 359/359 with 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines across all 31 reported authored source files, including the final 500-sequence state model. The subsequent packed-consumer acceptance failed its explicit file allowlist because the new documented example and validation JSON were intentionally added to package contents but omitted from that test. Updating only those exact allowlisted paths and required-file assertions. Also exercising the new exported reuse SDK and native TOON/JSON reuse command in both independent packed npm and Bun consumers. Full release gates will be rerun after the focused acceptance check."
  "2026-10-26T01:12:58.782Z",codex-agent,"Focused packed acceptance passed 2/2 after the exact allowlist correction, including the new exported SDK and both native output formats under npm and Bun. Final provenance review also found that authenticating a stored call label alone would let a modified root label/digest claim an old request asked a different question. Reuse now verifies every original call digest and reserved prompt against the native prompt builder before accepting it. Digest, relabeled question, depth and prompt tamper probes plus failed-child accounting passed 2/2. With only that verifier disabled, the tamper test failed with a missing expected refusal; exact source was restored. This strengthens the explicit question/tool identity acceptance boundary without adding storage or model calls."
